# API Keys Configuration
#
# Copy this file to .env, then UNCOMMENT and fill in only the lines you have
# credentials for:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Every line below is commented out on purpose. A variable set to a placeholder
# value is worse than one that is absent: an unset optional key costs you
# nothing but a lower rate limit, whereas a literal "your_..._here" is sent to
# the API as if it were real and the request is rejected outright — e.g. NCBI
# answers HTTP 400 {"error":"API key invalid"} and PubMed then returns no
# papers at all, while every other source keeps working.
#
# The loader detects the known placeholder patterns and ignores them with a
# warning, but leaving a line commented out is cleaner than relying on that.

# --- Search sources ---------------------------------------------------------

# Scopus (required for Scopus searches)
# Get from: https://dev.elsevier.com/
#SCOPUS_API_KEY=

# PubMed / Unpaywall email (required for PubMed searches and for downloads)
# Any valid email address — free, no registration
#PUBMED_EMAIL=

# PubMed API key (OPTIONAL — only raises the rate limit from 3 to 10 req/sec)
# Leave commented out unless you actually have one.
# Get from: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/account/
#PUBMED_API_KEY=

# IEEE Xplore (OPTIONAL — only needed if 'ieee' is in config.yaml sources)
# Get from: https://developer.ieee.org/
#IEEE_API_KEY=

# --- Downloads --------------------------------------------------------------

# Unpaywall email (OPTIONAL — falls back to PUBMED_EMAIL when unset)
#UNPAYWALL_EMAIL=

# Zotero translation server (OPTIONAL — primary PDF fetcher when running)
# Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:1969 if not set.
# Set up once with: python scripts/setup_zotero.py
#ZOTERO_TRANSLATION_SERVER=http://127.0.0.1:1969
